{"type":"text","timestamp":1794872767619,"sessionID":"ses_e193f3330ffeih7BC9i0XRd5Kp","part":{"id":"prt_1e6c0f2b9001ypMzM2etxXNclU","messageID":"msg_1e6c0d9db0019oJWtdJGUjwYYs","sessionID":"ses_e193f3330ffeih7BC9i0XRd5Kp","type":"text","text":"Let me understand the issue better. The `cmd_check_anchors` function processes anchor files that exist, but doesn't verify that every attested range head (from `.sigstore.json` files) has a corresponding `.ots` proof file. I need to add this check.\n","time":{"start":1794872767161,"end":1794872767617}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794872767631,"sessionID":"ses_e193f3330ffeih7BC9i0XRd5Kp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call-08562d80-79d5-403f-b21d-a7fa5d18cd5d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/record/record.py","offset":383,"limit":50},"output":"<path>/workspace/record/record.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n383: def cmd_check_anchors(a):\n384:     \"\"\"Every anchor must be right, and the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap.\n385:     Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n386:     chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n387:     rows, bad, cant, ranges = [], [], [], []\n388:     for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n389:         n = os.path.basename(path)\n390:         m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n391:         seq = int(m.group(1))\n392:         try:\n393:             if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\n394:                 raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n395:             raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n396:             if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n397:                 t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n398:                 rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n399:             else:\n400:                 t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n401:                 if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n402:                         or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n403:                     raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n404:                 ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n405:                 rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n406:                              \"writer_commit\": commit})\n407:         except Bad as ex:\n408:             bad.append(str(ex))\n409:         except CantCheck as ex:\n410:             cant.append(f\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\")\n411:     covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n412:     for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n413:         if lo != covered + 1:\n414:             bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n415:         covered = max(covered, hi)\n416:         if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n417:             changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n418:                             \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n419:         prev_commit = commit\n420:     if covered < len(chain):\n421:         bad.append(f\"entries {covered + 1}-{len(chain)} were never attested by the writer\")\n422:     print(json.dumps({\"anchors\": rows, \"entries\": len(chain), \"writer_attested_through\": covered,\n423:                       \"writer_runs\": changes, \"wrong\": bad, \"could_not_check\": cant}, indent=1))\n424:     for x in bad:\n425:         print(f\"BAD: {x}\", file=sys.stderr)\n426:     for x in cant:\n427:         print(f\"CAN'T CHECK: {x}\", file=sys.stderr)\n428:     return 1 if bad else 2 if cant else 0\n429: \n430: \n431: def _git(a, *args):\n432:     root = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(a.ledger))\n\n(Showing lines 383-432 of 630. Use offset=433 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"def cmd_check_anchors(a):\n    \"\"\"Every anchor must be right, and the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap.\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges = [], [], [], []\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\n        try:\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\n                raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n            if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n            else:\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/record/record.py","text":"def cmd_check_anchors(a):\n    \"\"\"Every anchor must be right, and the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap.\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges = [], [], [], []\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\n        try:\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\n                raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n            if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n            else:\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                    raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n                ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                             \"writer_commit\": commit})\n        except Bad as ex:\n            bad.append(str(ex))\n        except CantCheck as ex:\n            cant.append(f\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\")\n    covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if lo != covered + 1:\n            bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n        covered = max(covered, hi)\n        if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n            changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                            \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n        prev_commit = commit\n    if covered < len(chain):\n        bad.append(f\"entries {covered + 1}-{len(chain)} were never attested by the writer\")\n    print(json.dumps({\"anchors\": rows, \"entries\": len(chain), \"writer_attested_through\": covered,\n                      \"writer_runs\": changes, \"wrong\": bad, \"could_not_check\": cant}, indent=1))\n    for x in bad:\n        print(f\"BAD: {x}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    for x in cant:\n        print(f\"CAN'T CHECK: {x}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    return 1 if bad else 2 if cant else 0\n\n\ndef _git(a, *args):\n    root = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(a.ledger))","lineStart":383,"lineEnd":432,"totalLines":630,"truncated":true}},"title":"workspace/record/record.py","time":{"start":1794872767615,"end":1794872767622}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me analyze the issue. The bug report says that `check-anchors` misses a deleted OpenTimestamps proof. When a `.sigstore.json` file exists for a range head (e.g., `anchors/000002.sigstore.json` attesting the range ending at entry 2), but the corresponding `.ots` proof file is missing, `check-anchors` still exits 0 instead of reporting the missing proof.\n\nLooking at the `cmd_check_anchors` function (lines 383-428), I can see:\n1. It iterates through all files in the `anchors` directory matching the pattern\n2. For each file, it checks if it's an `.ots` or `.sigstore.json` file\n3. For `.sigstore.json` files, it verifies the attestation and collects ranges\n4. For `.ots` files, it verifies the proof\n\nThe issue is that the code only processes anchor files that exist. It doesn't check if there's a `.sigstore.json` file for a range head that should have a corresponding `.ots` file but doesn't.\n\nThe requirement is:\n- `check-anchors` must exit 1 when the `.ots` proof for any attested range head is missing\n- It must print a message to stderr containing `NNNNNN.ots is missing`\n- With the proof present, existing behavior must not change\n\nSo I need to:\n1. After collecting all the sigstore ranges, check if each range head (the `to_seq` in each range) has a corresponding `.ots` file\n2. If not, add an error message and exit with code 1\n\nLet me look at the test file to see if there are any existing tests for check-anchors that I need to be aware of. There's one test at line 218-223: `test_check_anchors_requires_the_writer_to_cover_every_entry`.\n\nNow let me implement the fix. I'll modify the `cmd_check_anchors` function to check for missing `.ots` files for each attested range head.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e6c0f47c001y9DHnk6GZ6JnFd","sessionID":"ses_e193f3330ffeih7BC9i0XRd5Kp","messageID":"msg_1e6c0d9db0019oJWtdJGUjwYYs"}}
